The inference of calls to builtins such as ``type()``, ``len()``, ``list()`` or
``dict.fromkeys()`` no longer applies when the name refers to a parameter, a
variable or an import that shadows the builtin, as in ``def f(x, type): return
type(x)``; the call is inferred through the shadowing definition instead.

Closes pylint-dev/pylint#10994
